For purposes of applying the Check Act, the persons or institutions deemed equivalent to banks shall be as follows:
1. Post offices;
2. Regional agricultural cooperatives engaged in credit business under Article 57 (1) 3 of the Agricultural Cooperatives Act;
3. Regional livestock cooperatives engaged in credit business under Article 106 (3) of the Agricultural Cooperatives Act;
4. Cooperatives by commodity or business type engaged in credit business under Article 14 of the Addenda to the Agricultural Cooperatives Act, Act No. 6018;
5. District fisheries cooperatives engaged in credit business under Article 60 (1) 3 of the Fisheries Cooperatives Act;
6. Deleted on October 25, 2016;
7. Fisheries cooperatives by business type and fisheries cooperatives for processing fishery products engaged in credit business under Article 5 of the Addenda to the Act Partially Amending the Fisheries Cooperatives Act, Act No. 4820;
8. The National Federation of Community Credit Cooperatives engaged in credit business under Article 67 (1) 5 of the Community Credit Cooperatives Act;
9. The Federation of Mutual Savings Banks engaged in business under Article 25-2 (1) of the Mutual Savings Banks Act;
10. The National Credit Union Federation engaged in credit business under Article 78 (1) 5 of the Credit Unions Act.
